# Unanchored: the root install and legacy/'s. Never `git add -f` one — a worktree's link to
# the main checkout's install went in that way once and became a symlink to itself (#210).
node_modules
shots/_*
# A blind pair is two copies of shots that are already committed — ours at
# shots/<piece>/r<N>-<state>-ours.png and the opponent's under shots/oracle/ —
# laid out under letters a critic is shown. The round says which letter was ours,
# so the pair can be laid out again; committing it would only double the bytes.
shots/blind/
# Claude Code's project settings and hooks are the repo's (a worktree needs the
# hook script too); its worktrees and local overrides are not.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
*.pkg.tar.zst
# makepkg's build directories, at the root only: unanchored, `src/` would
# swallow `quill/src/` and `quill-engine/src/`.
/src/
/pkg/
target/
# Exploratory scratch crates, kept out of the repo.
/spike/
# Python bytecode caches, wherever they land.
__pycache__/
